Krita Nova 11 - "Brush Settings" title bar on the brush editor panel (Android)

The brush editor popup (KisPopupButtonFrame, Qt::Popup) was drawn with a
QFrame::Box | Plain frame. A plain box uses the text color, so on dark themes
the panel had a white border.

1. KisPopupButton::setPopupTitleBar(title): the frame gets a bar on top in the
   panel's own color (QPalette::Window), with the title centered and a
   finger-sized close button (icon window-close) on the right that hides the
   popup. A frame with a title bar has no box border. adjustPosition() adds the
   bar's height to the popup size.
2. On Android, a frame with a title bar is a frameless window: Krita's
   Android Qt draws its own white frame (with a thicker top edge to drag by)
   around decorated windows, which was the remaining white border. Dragging
   the title bar moves the window instead.
3. KisPaintopBox: on Android, the brush editor uses the title "Brush Settings".
   Desktop builds are unchanged.

